  "publication_day": "2026-07-10",
  "article_opening": "Price change for Nvidia stock in last 1 year: 24%\n$NVDA Stock Price as of Jul. 9: $203\n52-Week High: $236\n$NVDA Stock Price Target: $302\nTD Cowen reiterated its Buy rating on Nvidia ( NVDA ) stock and named it a Top Pick, maintaining a $275 price target implying roughly 35% upside from where shares closed.\nThe call came after the firm hosted an investor lunch with Nvidia’s leadership team, including CEO Jensen Huang, CFO Colette Kress, and Head of Investor Relations Toshiya Hari.\nAnalyst Joshua ",
  "passage": "…pic.\nMeanwhile, TD Cowen estimates that Nvidia’s revenue from enterprise applications across multiple industries is in the low-to-mid-teens range.\nThat’s a meaningful chunk of business coming from outside the flashy AI chatbot headlines, which is part of Buchalter’s point about Nvidia’s opportunity being underappreciated.\nTD Cowen also highlighted evidence that computing capacity is genuinely tight right now. Rental prices for older GPU models have been climbing, AI adoption continues to widen across industries, and recent cloud computing deals have been signed at premium prices.\nAll of that points to demand outpacing supply.\nNvidia’s own recent quarterly results back up the strength story.\nThe company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, marking its third straight quarter of accelerating growth.\nData center revenue alone hit $75 billion, up 92% year over year.\nNvidia also highlighted a new growth driver: its Vera CPU line, which the company expects to generate $20 billion in sales by the end of this fiscal year, a notable push into a market historically dominated by Intel and AMD.\nBeyond the CPU expansion, Nvidia has been striking new partnerships, including a deal with Valar Atomics to build a nuclear-powered data center in Utah aimed at reducing water use for AI computing.\nAI startup Perplexity has also chosen to use Nvidia’s new CPUs for AI agent tasks.\nSee analysts’ growth forecasts and price targets for Nvidia stock (It’s free) >>>\nWhat the Market Is Telling Us About Nvidia St…",
  "statement": "The company posted $82 billion in total revenue, up 85% year-over-year, marking its third straight quarter of accelerating growth."
 },
 {
