  "passage": "In a move that underscores the growing convergence of advanced computing hardware and enterprise software platforms, Nvidia ( NVDA +2.48% ) and Palantir Technologies ( PLTR +1.34% ) announced a collaboration designed to bring powerful open AI models into highly sensitive, classified environments.\nThe collaboration targets U.S. government agencies -- where data control, security requirements, and customization are nonnegotiable. By combining open-source flexibility with innovative safeguards, Nvidia and Palantir aim to accelerate the adoption of artificial intelligence (AI) without compromising national security or operational integrity.\nHow are Nvidia and Palantir working together?\nThe partnership features Palantir's new intelligence engine, which deploys Nvidia's Nemotron open models within secure, sovereign systems inside customers' own environments. The engine is built on Palantir's Sovereign AI Operating System, which integrates the company's Artificial Intelligence Platform (AI…",
  "statement": "Nvidia ( NVDA +2.48% ) and Palantir Technologies ( PLTR +1.34% ) announced a collaboration designed to bring powerful open AI models into highly sensitive, classified environments."
 },
 {
  "id": "G458",
  "article_id": "gnews:07610e55de6cc86b2b508b1d",
  "title": "NVIDIA Nemotron Achieves Benchmark-Leading Performance With LangChain Deep Agents Harness",
  "publication_day": "2026-07-08",
  "article_opening": "Tuning the LangChain Deep Agents harness for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra delivers leading performance and faster task completion on an open stack that enterprises can run, customize and control.\nNVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra is offering leading performance at lower cost than top closed models with the largest and most widely adopted AI agent orchestration platform.\nLangChain tuned its Deep Agents harness for NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Ultra, achieving the highest accuracy among open models, while completing more t",
  "passage": "…dels , tools and runtime — tuned for their own workflows. It combines LangChain Deep Agents Code, tuned for Nemotron 3 Ultra, with the NVIDIA OpenShell secure runtime for executing agent actions safely.\nAn open model, an open harness and an open secure runtime means enterprises own the full stack, end to end. They can customize it around the expertise that sets their business apart, keep improving it and run it anywhere — their own infrastructure, their own cloud, their own governance.\nThat distinction matters more as agents take on higher-stakes work. The shift from AI assistants that answer questions to agents that take action inside core systems changes what businesses get from their AI.\nNemoClaw for LangChain Deep Agents and the tuned Nemotron 3 Ultra model profile are available now . Developers can pull the tuned Deep Agents harness directly from LangChain, or use the NemoClaw for LangChain Deep Agents blueprint as a starting point for building specialized agents from scratch.\nLangChain developers can access Nemotron 3 Ultra on Baseten , Crusoe Cloud , DeepInfra, Fireworks , Nebius and Together AI platforms, giving them a direct, hosted path to the tuned harness in production.\nEY can help enterprises start building their own specialized agents today, using this open software stack.\nLearn more about NVIDIA NemoClaw for LangChain Deep Agents and NVIDIA Nemotron.\nExplore self-paced video tutorials and livestreams .",
  "statement": "NemoClaw for LangChain Deep Agents and the tuned Nemotron 3 Ultra model profile are available now"
 },
 {
  "id": "G410",
  "article_id": "gnews:bf96def37a9c3a5f19f5d43c",
  "title": "LG Electronics to Build Nvidia AI Server Racks",
  "publication_day": "2026-07-12",
  "article_opening": "By Lee Seok-jin\nLG Electronics (066570.KS) is developing an AI chip-based server rack targeting Nvidia and plans to begin mass production next year. The move expands the recent AI infrastructure alliance between LG and Nvidia into server rack manufacturing.\nAccording to the semiconductor industry on the 12th, LG Electronics' Production Research Institute (PRI) completed development of an AI server rack prototype matching the compute tray specifications of Nvidia's \"Vera Rubin\" in the first half ",
  "passage": "…d the cooling technology accumulated over 58 years, since it launched Korea's first home air conditioner in 1968, to its AI racks. Already holding air-cooling and water-cooling technologies for AI servers, LG Electronics applied a \"direct-to-chip (DTC)\" cooling method to this AI rack, circulating coolant around the chips to control heat generation.\nAI server rack manufacturing is the final piece that will complete LG Group's data center turnkey strategy. LG is targeting the AI data center construction market with its \"One LG\" strategy, which combines LG Electronics' heating, ventilation and air conditioning, LG Energy Solution's batteries, and LG CNS's data center construction capabilities. LG Chairman Kwang-mo Koo is known to have discussed expanding data center cooperation, including AI rack supply, with Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, who visited the company's Yeouido headquarters last month.\n\"With server rack development, LG will cover all areas of AI data centers except the chip and power sectors,\" an industry official said.\nAI-translated from Korean. Quotes from foreign sources are based on Korean-language reports and may not reflect exact original wording.\nAn English ontology of the Korean market — how companies, the media, the government and the National Assembly move each other in a loop. Korea's named controlling persons and designated business groups are a mechanism, not a risk to be priced blind.\nA live, cap-weighted view of every KOSPI and KOSDAQ sector, with same-day Korean reporting distilled by company — built for foreign investors, correspondents and analysts who n…",
  "statement": "LG Chairman Kwang-mo Koo is known to have discussed expanding data center cooperation, including AI rack supply, with Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang, who visited the company's Yeouido headquarters last month."
 },
 {
