  "article_opening": "Greg Lui Arrested Over Alleged $300 Million Nvidia Server Smuggling to China\nGreg Lui of Earthmade is accused of shipping over $300 million in Nvidia servers to China through Malaysia and Singapore, federal prosecutors say.\nGreg Lui, 38, owner of California-based Earthmade Computer, was arrested on October 1, 2026 on charges of sending servers with Nvidia chips worth more than $300 million to China, sidestepping U.S. export licenses through two stopovers in Malaysia and Singapore. The Department",
  "passage": "Greg Lui Arrested Over Alleged $300 Million Nvidia Server Smuggling to China\nGreg Lui of Earthmade is accused of shipping over $300 million in Nvidia servers to China through Malaysia and Singapore, federal prosecutors say.\nGreg Lui, 38, owner of California-based Earthmade Computer, was arrested on October 1, 2026 on charges of sending servers with Nvidia chips worth more than $300 million to China, sidestepping U.S. export licenses through two stopovers in Malaysia and Singapore. The Department of Justice (DOJ) disclosed the case in a press release, but it remains an allegation and Lui is presumed innocent until a verdict.\nThe grand jury indictment (the panel that decides whether a case goes to trial), filed on September 29 at the federal court in Los Angeles, yields flight dates, order numbers and airline names. Such details are rare in a case like this, and they let readers follow the servers step by step.\n…",
